course: dictionary
lesson: 13219
title: Gab: talking and chatter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To gab means to talk a lot, quickly, about small things. It is an informal word, so you would use it with friends and family, not in a formal letter. «The girls gabbed about their new shoes all the way home.» Here gabbed is a verb: they talked and talked about small things.
explain: Gab can also be a noun. «Her gab kept us awake until midnight.» Here gab means her chatter, her endless talking. The words around it, like kept us awake, are the clues that tell you it is about talk.
explain: Some people have a special skill with words. «The salesman had the gift of the gab, and he sold us a bike we did not need.» Here gab means the ability to talk easily and persuade people. In the US, people say «the gift of gab».
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. Try swapping in chatter or natter: if the sentence still makes sense, you have got it.
fact: Gab means to talk a lot about unimportant things; it means to chatter.
fact: Gab is an informal word, so keep it for chatty talk with friends, not for formal writing.
fact: The verb forms are gab, gabs, gabbed and gabbing: «She gabs all day.» «They gabbed for an hour.»
fact: «The gift of the gab» (UK) or «the gift of gab» (US) means being able to talk easily and persuade people.
fact: Related words: chatter, natter (UK) and yak all mean talking a lot.
exercise: «The girls gabbed about their new shoes all the way home.» What does gabbed mean here? | Walked very fast | Argued angrily | *Talked a lot about small things | Sang loudly
exercise: «Her gab kept us awake until midnight.» In this sentence, what does gab mean? | A hungry dog | A gap in a wall | A loud bang | *Chatter, endless talking
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to gab? | *Natter | Sleep | Shout | Hide
test: «The salesman had the gift of the gab, and he sold us a bike we did not need.» What does the gift of the gab mean? | Being good at sport | Having a loud voice | *Being able to talk easily and persuade people | Knowing lots of jokes
test: Which sentence uses gab as a verb? | «She had a big gab about her holiday.» | *«He gabs with his friends every lunchtime.» | «Her gab was a gift.» | «The gab was very loud.»
exam: Which word is too informal for a formal letter to a headteacher? | Dear | Thank you | *Gab | Sincerely
